L414: ### cite109†Scoped and Read-Only Filesystems L415: 
L416: Scoped disks allow you to define a filesystem where all paths are automatically prefixed with a given path prefix. Before creating a scoped filesystem disk, you will need to install an additional Flysystem package via the Composer package manager:
L417: 
L418:     `
L419: 
L420:     1 composer require league/flysystem-path-prefixing "^3.0"
L421: 
L422: 
L423:     composer require league/flysystem-path-prefixing "^3.0"
L424: 
L425:     `
L426: You may create a path scoped instance of any existing filesystem disk by defining a disk that utilizes the `scoped` driver. For example, you may create a disk which scopes your existing `s3` disk to a specific path prefix, and then every file operation using your scoped disk will utilize the specified prefix:
L427: 
L428:     `
L429: 
L430:     1's3-videos' => [
L431: 
L432:     2    'driver' => 'scoped',
L433: 
L434:     3    'disk' => 's3',
L435: 
L436:     4    'prefix' => 'path/to/videos',
L437: 
L438:     5],
L439: 
L440: 
L441:     's3-videos' => [
L442:         'driver' => 'scoped',
L443:         'disk' => 's3',
L444:         'prefix' => 'path/to/videos',
L445:     ],
L446: 
L447:     `
L448: "Read-only" disks allow you to create filesystem disks that do not allow write operations. Before using the `read-only` configuration option, you will need to install an additional Flysystem package via the Composer package manager:
L449: 
L450:     `
L451: 
L452:     1 composer require league/flysystem-read-only "^3.0"
L453: 
L454: 
L455:     composer require league/flysystem-read-only "^3.0"
L456: 
L457:     `
L458: Next, you may include the `read-only` configuration option in one or more of your disk's configuration arrays:
L459: 
L460:     `
L461: 
L462:     1's3-videos' => [
L463: 
L464:     2    'driver' => 's3',
L465: 
L466:     3    // ...
L467: 
L468:     4    'read-only' => true,
L469: 
L470:     5],
L471: 
L472: 
L473:     's3-videos' => [
L474:         'driver' => 's3',
L475:         // ...
L476:         'read-only' => true,
L477:     ],
L478: 
L479:     `
L480: ### cite110†Amazon S3 Compatible Filesystems L481: By default, your application's `filesystems` configuration file contains a disk configuration for the `s3` disk. In addition to using this disk to interact with cite132†Amazon S3†aws.amazon.com , you may use it to interact with any S3-compatible file storage service such as cite133†RustFS†github.com , cite134†DigitalOcean Spaces†www.digitalocean.com , cite135†Vultr Object Storage†www.vultr.com , cite136†Cloudflare R2†www.cloudflare.com , or cite137†Hetzner Cloud Storage†www.hetzner.com .
